From 55f4b6a43564c478fea26abcbeaac63cbd268384 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Dannenmuller <thomas.dannenmuller@opendigitaleducation.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:04:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ath79: add a powerline key service and port 2 for TP-Link
 Deco P9

The Deco P9 powerline chip is a Broadcom part behind switch port 2. It
speaks a vendor protocol over raw Ethernet frames (ethertype 0x8912, OUI
00:1F:84), not the Qualcomm one used by open-plc-utils.

Add the plc-bcm package: a ucode tool and a procd service that write the
network membership key from /etc/config/plc to the chip at boot, only when
it differs. The default key is the standard HomePlug AV one, so two new
devices see each other out of the box; it should be changed.

Put port 2 in the LAN by default for this board, and install plc-bcm in the
default image. The protocol was decoded from the stock firmware and tested
on a Deco P9; the image itself has not been built or booted.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Dannenmuller <thomas.dannenmuller@opendigitaleducation.com>
